    "proved": [
      "For all transverse polarizations on symmetric N, full-NS support invariance is equivalent to closure of noncollinear sums. For real span dimension at least two this is equivalent to N union zero being an additive subgroup. Collinear and empty exceptions are retained. Failure has a fixed smooth real finite datum and actual local NS leakage with strict o(t).",
